the knowledge base jerseycharities includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/jerseyCharities.l4".

a place is BOT if
    the english name of the place is "Anguilla"
    or the english name of the place is "Bermuda"
    or the english name of the place is "British Antarctic Territory"
    or the english name of the place is "British Indian Ocean Territory"
    or the english name of the place is "Cayman Islands"
    or the english name of the place is "Falkland Islands"
    or the english name of the place is "Gibraltar"
    or the english name of the place is "Hong Kong"
    or the english name of the place is "Montserrat"
    or the english name of the place is "Pitcairn, Henderson, Ducie and Oeno Islands"
    or the english name of the place is "St Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha"
    or the english name of the place is "Sovereign Base Areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia"
    or the english name of the place is "South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands"
    or the english name of the place is "Turks and Caicos Islands"
    or the english name of the place is "Virgin Islands".

qualifying territory for a place if
    the place is BOT
    and it is not the case that the english name of the place is "Sovereign Base Areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia".

section section 5 charity test is:

the known charitable purposes is ["the prevention or relief of poverty", "the advancement of education", "the advancement of religion", "the advancement of health", "the saving of lives", "the advancement of citizenship or community development", "the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science", "the advancement of public participation in sport", "the provision of recreational facilities, or the organisation of recreational activities, with the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom the facilities or activities are primarily intended", "the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation", "the promotion of religious or racial harmony", "the promotion of equality and diversity", "the advancement of environmental protection or improvement", "the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage", "the advancement of animal welfare", "something analogous to one of the above"].

a value is charitable if
    the known charitable purposes is a list
    and the value is in the list.

all purposes are qualifying for an entity if
    the purposes of the entity is a list
    and for all cases in which
        a value is in the list
        it is the case that
            the value is charitable
            or the value is analogous to charitable purpose
            or the value is ancillary.

an entity meets the charity test if
    all purposes are qualifying for the entity
    and the entity provides public benefit in jersey else elsewhere
    and it is not the case that
        directed by minister for the entity
        or directed by states assembly member for the entity
        or directed by equivalent in another jurisdiction for the entity.

eligible for registration as charity for an entity if
    the entity meets the charity test
    and the constitution for the entity is a constitution
    and the constitution is a written document
    and the entity is a jersey entity
        or carries out substantial activity in jersey for the entity
    and the entity has a principal address in jersey.

