%   source: lines 363-370
% no LE form found: ((`same as another charity` OF `n`) OR (`too similar to another charity` OF `n`) OR (`misleading` OF `n`) OR (`implies false connection` OF `n`) OR (`offensi...
%   l4:
%   | GIVEN n IS A Name
%   | GIVETH A BOOLEAN
%   | DECIDE `is undesirable` IF
%   |     `same as another charity` n
%   |     OR `too similar to another charity` n
%   |     OR `misleading` n
%   |     OR `implies false connection` n
%   |     OR `offensive` n
% RESIDUE r1 END

eligible for restricted section for an entity if
    eligible for registration as charity for the entity
    and requested restricted section for the entity
    and the entity meets funding condition
        or refrains from soliciting donations for the entity.

complies with requirements for an entity if
    the entity is registered
    and reports changes for the entity
    and the entity provides annual return
    and the entity meets funding condition
        or it is not the case that the registration section for the entity is restricted_section
        or refrains from soliciting donations for the entity
    and it is not the case that amended to non charitable purpose for the entity
    and it is not the case that changed name without permission for the entity
    and it is not the case that uses other than registered name for the entity
    and it is not the case that amended purposes without approval for the entity
    and it is not the case that amended statement without approval for the entity
    and applies property per purposes for the entity
    and applies property per statement for the entity.

fulfills governor duties for a person with an entity if
    the person is governor of for the entity
    and the entity is registered
    and acts with due diligence for the person with the entity
    and acts as prudent person for the person with the entity
    and acts to best ability for the person with the entity
    and observes good faith for the person with the entity
    and ensures consistency with purposes for the person with the entity
    and ensures compliance with law for the person with the entity
    and reported to charity for the person with the entity
        and reported to commissioner for the person
        or it is not the case that reportable matter exists for the person
        or declared no reportable matters for the person with the entity.

an entity may refer to as jersey charity for an user if
    the entity is registered
    and the entity is a jersey entity
    and wholly managed in jersey for the entity
    or it is not the case that
        knows not registered for the user with the entity
        and intends to mislead for the user with the entity
            or intends to gain advantage for the user with the entity.

an entity may refer to as charity for an user if
    the entity is registered
    or it is not the case that
        knows not registered for the user with the entity
        and intends to mislead for the user with the entity
            or intends to gain advantage for the user with the entity.

% RESIDUE r2 BEGIN: excepted foreign charity
% TODO: translate the fragment below by hand, or with the Contract Assistant (residue mode); it was not translated automatically
%   source: lines 476-488
% no LE form found: (((`established under UK law` OF `entity`) OR (`established under prescribed law` OF `entity`)) AND (`entitled to use charity term` OF `entity`) AND (`manage...
%   l4:
%   | GIVEN entity IS AN Entity
%   | GIVETH A BOOLEAN
%   | DECIDE `excepted foreign charity` IF
%   |     -- First condition - established under relevant law
%   |     (
%   |         `established under UK law` entity
%   |         OR `established under prescribed law` entity
%   |     )
%   |     -- Entitled to refer to itself as charity in that jurisdiction
%   |     AND `entitled to use charity term` entity
%   |     -- Second condition - managed from that jurisdiction and not registered
%   |     AND `managed from establishment jurisdiction` entity
%   |     AND NOT `is registered` entity
% RESIDUE r2 END

an entity may issue required steps notice if
    the entity is registered
    and misconduct for the entity
        or it is not the case that the entity meets the charity test
        or governor misconduct for the entity
        or governor reportable matter for the entity
        or it is not the case that
            the entity is a jersey entity
            or carries out substantial activity in jersey for the entity
        or it is not the case that the entity has a principal address in jersey.

an entity may deregister if
    the entity is registered
    and applied for deregistration for the entity
        or it is not the case that the entity meets the charity test
        or misled commissioner for the entity
        or required steps notice served for the entity
            and it is not the case that complied with notice for the entity
        or no longer exists for the entity.

an entity must apply a property for preserved purposes if
    the entity is deregistered
    and acquired before deregistration for the property.

% RESIDUE r3 BEGIN: may appeal to tribunal
% TODO: translate the fragment below by hand, or with the Contract Assistant (residue mode); it was not translated automatically
%   source: lines 540-564
% no LE form found: (((`applied for registration` OF `entity`) AND (`is registration refusal` OF `decision`)) OR ((`is registered` OF `entity`) AND (`is deregistration decision`...
%   l4:
%   | GIVEN entity IS AN Entity
%   |       decision IS A Decision
%   | GIVETH A BOOLEAN
%   | DECIDE `may appeal to tribunal` IF
%   |     (
%   |         -- Applicant appealing registration refusal
%   |         `applied for registration` entity
%   |         AND `is registration refusal` decision
%   |     )
%   |     OR (
%   |         -- Charity appealing deregistration
%   |         `is registered` entity
%   |         AND `is deregistration decision` decision
%   |     )
%   |     OR (
%   |         -- Charity appealing name change refusal
%   |         `is registered` entity
%   |         AND `applied to change name` entity
%   |         AND `is name change refusal` decision
%   |     )
%   |     OR (
%   |         -- Entity or person appealing required steps notice
%   |         (`is registered` entity OR `governor of registered charity` entity)
%   |         AND `is required steps notice` decision
%   |     )
% RESIDUE r3 END

a person may disclose for an info if
    in public register for the info
    or general section for the info
    or restricted section public elements for the info
    or historic section for the info
    or disclosure to authorized person for the info
    or for investigation of offense for the info
    or for legal proceedings for the info.

an entity may require governor removal for a notice if
    the entity may issue required steps notice
    and it is not the case that organized religious charity for the entity.

